# Template for .argent/secrets.env — copy, then fill in real values:
#
#   cp .argent/secrets.env.example .argent/secrets.env
#
# .argent/secrets.env is gitignored. This .example file IS committed so the
# required names are discoverable, so it must never contain real values.
#
# Flows reference these as {{secret:NAME}}. The tool-server resolves them at run
# time and never prints a value. Confirm they are picked up with:
#
#   bunx argent secrets
#
# Only secrets belong here. The Kinde test environment's domain, client id and
# audience are not secrets — they belong in the app/server .env files.
#
# ── Use the Kinde TEST environment, never production. ────────────────────────


# The test user that E2E flows sign in as.
#
# Both platforms redirect to Kinde's hosted login page (web via the server's
# /api/login redirect, native via @kinde/expo PKCE in a browser sheet), so one
# email/password pair covers both.
#
# This account should exist ONLY in the Kinde test environment and own no data
# you care about — flows create and delete expenses as this user.
KINDE_TEST_EMAIL=
KINDE_TEST_PASSWORD=


# ── Optional, add only if a flow actually needs it ───────────────────────────
#
# A second user, for proving one account cannot see another's expenses from the
# UI. The integration tests already cover this at the API level with two users,
# so add these only if you want the same proof end to end.
# KINDE_TEST_EMAIL_B=
# KINDE_TEST_PASSWORD_B=
#
# A TOTP seed, if you enable MFA on the test environment. Leave MFA off there if
# you can — it is the main reason interactive-login flows turn flaky.
# KINDE_TEST_TOTP_SECRET=
